Optional runtime dependency, imported only from src/vesper/crypto.py:
  ecdsa on PyPI (often called python-ecdsa). MIT License.
  It is not copied into this tree. Install it from PyPI.
  The project metadata of that package carries its copyright notice.

If that import fails, the kernel uses HMAC-SHA256 from the Python standard
library. No extra notice is required for the fallback.

Cryptography in this project is limited to SHA-256, HMAC-SHA256, and
ECDSA P-256 (secp256r1).
